City's UAE owners could exit amid cheating charges. That would pose a challenge for a city — and prime minister — closely tied to Abu Dhabi.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Football: German coach Hürzeler flying high in Premier League</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:55746ba2aa6702d0257e08a3eece660765fbb9e1fb31a8638d6b406ca8b87f41</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:14:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T06:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/football-german-coach-h_rzeler-flying-high-in-premier-league/a-79714763--701507a044eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/football-german-coach-hürzeler-flying-high-in-premier-league/a-79714763?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fabian Hürzeler is younger than his star player, a fellow Premier League German. But, contrary to his reputation in his homeland, Hürzeler has become a popular figure both on and off the pitch in England.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Formula One in Rwanda: Sportswashing claims vs. hopes for African legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7551e53cf3dc4ea7cd58d404b07502edcfeb53ee93b89fa6683500eeb0c10e83</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:14:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T08:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/formula-one-in-rwanda-sportswashing-claims-vs-hopes-for-african-legacy/a-79650744--59b33a158fd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/formula-one-in-rwanda-sportswashing-claims-vs-hopes-for-african-legacy/a-79650744?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Formula One will return to Africa for the first time since 1993. There is concern Rwanda are using it as another sportswashing opportunity, but there is also hope the event's legacy can impact wider African society.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>FIFPRO report highlights growing pains in women's football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8002135decd4c7b4f8d25697f55d99b0031310967d83abd5050d2e411b6f21a5</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:14:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T08:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifpro-report-highlights-growing-pains-in-women-s-football/a-79648013--365fa34aee7b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifpro-report-highlights-growing-pains-in-women-s-football/a-79648013?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Expected global revenue of over $1 billion and new faces at the U17 World Cup show women's football is booming, but a recent report also highlights need for better structures globally.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Formula 1: Rwanda to bring sport back to Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb450a85bf6465577ad00a412c52af93855ad4004075b91a3420b01524e95447</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:14:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T11:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/formula-1-rwanda-to-bring-sport-back-to-africa/a-79649217--ee284b399c6d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/formula-1-rwanda-to-bring-sport-back-to-africa/a-79649217?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The last time Formula 1 hosted a race in Africa was way back in 1993. But a new track in Rwanda is set to host a Grand Prix in "the early 2030s," continuing the country’s investment in international sport.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's women: Ena Mahmutovic makes her case to become Germany's next No.1 goalkeeper</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a5f8605ad221f1a71cf0028b9aa42fb80dacb9f5408a39a7232cbacc84130c1</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:14:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T09:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-ena-mahmutovic-makes-her-case-to-become-germany-s-next-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79609341--71931b21638e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-ena-mahmutovic-makes-her-case-to-become-germany-s-next-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79609341?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's win against Australia saw Ena Mahmutovic excel in goal. The 22-year-old Bayern Munich goalkeeper is considered the successor to Ann-Katrin Berger and is making a name for herself.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>World Cup 2034: Does Saudi Arabia shelving Neom Stadium spell trouble?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9fb167618da8f90391088dfb2ee3fc5d1ced141b663db7dacf6f201d697a7aa3</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:14:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T11:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/world-cup-2034-does-saudi-arabia-shelving-neom-stadium-spell-trouble/a-79592948--b8b608a266b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/world-cup-2034-does-saudi-arabia-shelving-neom-stadium-spell-trouble/a-79592948?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since winning the right to hold the 2034 World Cup unopposed, Saudi Arabia has been pulling away from sport. With reports that its most ambitious stadium project will be abandoned, what does this mean for the World Cup?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ronaldo stays on under cloud as Messi exits internationals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d92e2688fcb2f0c3d88a0d0b6ff55040cdf7cef84a81b194e6c03e8238aa3085</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:14:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ronaldo-stays-on-under-cloud-as-messi-exits-internationals/a-79574551--518c4a71824f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ronaldo-stays-on-under-cloud-as-messi-exits-internationals/a-79574551?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Just hours before Lionel Messi played his last match for Argentina, Cristiano Ronaldo posted his latest salvo in a row with Portugal. Ronaldo wants to play on despite the troubles, while Messi bathed in adulation.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Munich up against at least six competitors for 2036 Olympics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6bcdc6b886d1317616750365d3d3c241402c2cfe9df98acabc19ee6589f5a8f</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:14:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/munich-up-against-at-least-six-competitors-for-2036-olympics/a-79566678--5b4a69f8bd09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/munich-up-against-at-least-six-competitors-for-2036-olympics/a-79566678?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The International Olympic Committee has revealed the six other countries intending to bid for the 2036 Olympic Games. This comes after Germany selected Munich as its Olympic candidate.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
